infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title traceparent vs tracestate
  desc One rigid universal identifier, one flexible vendor escape hatch
  compares
    - label traceparent
      children
        - label Fixed 55 bytes
          desc Four dash-separated fields, fixed width
        - label Universal identifier
          desc Same meaning for every vendor
        - label Parse without regex
          desc Split on dashes, check byte lengths
        - label trace-id is the join key
          desc 128-bit random; all-zeros invalid
        - label Invalid means fresh trace
          desc Unknown version or wrong length, start over
    - label tracestate
      children
        - label Vendor escape hatch
          desc Sampler, canary version, extra ids
        - label Up to 32 members
          desc key=value, up to 256 chars each
        - label 512+ chars propagated
          desc Pass through keys you do not understand
        - label Ordered list
          desc Prepend to add, move to front to update
        - label Never delete others' keys
          desc Preserves end-to-end vendor tracing
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
